# NestJS + FastAPI stack

Use the **latest stable** releases and official docs:

- NestJS: [docs.nestjs.com](https://docs.nestjs.com/)
- FastAPI: [fastapi.tiangolo.com](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/)
- React only if a frontend app is added later: [react.dev](https://react.dev/reference/react)

## Versions

Never hardcode versions from memory. Check current stable first:

```bash
source ~/.nvm/nvm.sh && nvm use 24.22.2 && npm view @nestjs/core version
# vision-engine (when scaffolding Python)
python3 --version   # prefer 3.11+
```

- Scaffold Nest: `npx @nestjs/cli@latest new <service>` under `services/`.
- Scaffold FastAPI under `services/vision-engine` with a pinned `requirements.txt` / lockfile (e.g. `uv` or `pip-tools`), not ad-hoc global installs.
- No `alpha`, `beta`, `rc`, `next`, or `canary`. Keep all `@nestjs/*` on the same major.

## NestJS (`api-gateway`, `worker-node`)

- Feature modules + DI; DTOs + `class-validator` + global `ValidationPipe`.
- Config via `@nestjs/config`; never hardcoded secrets.
- Queues: BullMQ (Redis) and/or Kafka for attendance / webhook jobs — handlers stay thin.
- Call `vision-engine` via an injected HTTP/gRPC client module, not by spawning Python.
- TypeScript strict mode.

## FastAPI (`vision-engine`)

- Async routes where I/O-bound; sync CPU vision work in thread/process pools so the event loop stays responsive.
- Pydantic models for request/response; OpenAPI from FastAPI defaults.
- OpenCV / DeepFace / RetinaFace stay inside this service only.
- Health endpoint for Compose readiness; accept image bytes or object-store references, return match scores / worker ids — never raw embedding vectors to untrusted clients unless `docs/main_plan.md` explicitly requires it.
